# Claude Code local state (agent worktrees, session scratch).
#
# Ignored by *contents* rather than as a directory, so that the one file meant to
# be shared can be re-included: git will not un-ignore a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so `.claude/` followed by `!.claude/settings.json` would
# silently do nothing.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# WSL / Windows alternate-data-stream artifacts
*:Zone.Identifier

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local env
.env

# The generated ADP client used to be ignored here, on the grounds that
# committing it would let a hand-edit survive regeneration. It is committed now,
# because `make check-generated` answers that worry directly: it regenerates
# from the vendored spec and fails on any difference, so a hand-edit dies in CI
# rather than living quietly in a working tree.
#
# Committing it buys three things the ignore could not. A clean `pip install`
# yields a working package with no generation step. The vendored spec and the
# code derived from it stay reviewable as a pair. And an ADP contract change
# arrives as a diff to that file in the pull request that bumps it, which is the
# loudest available form of "an ADP change breaks adp-replay loudly" (§2).

# Recorded trajectories, snapshots, and experiment output. These are large and
# content-addressed; they belong in a CAS root, not in git.
.adp-replay/
runs/
snapshots/
